      "message": "mmm I was just thinking of another scenario, but I don\u0027t think that\u0027s an issue either:\n1) A sends sync transaction to B\n2) As part of handling the transaction, B sends another sync transaction to C\n3) While C is handling the transaction, B dies\n4) C notices B is dead, and calls binder_send_failed_reply(), which calls binder_free_transaction()\n5) In parallel, we\u0027re cleaning up B and its threads, and free B\u0027s binder_proc\n\nbut the binder_free_transaction() we\u0027re calling in 4) is for the outgoing transaction from B, not the one coming into B. I think that transaction can only be cleaned up in the process itself, which presumably makes this safe?",
